contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789066325931,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"7cddc8c9f567cbddd7363d4a94679f277575098518a3081cc605bfaf95c9f3e7","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7cddc8c9f567cbddd7363d4a94679f277575098518a3081cc605bfaf95c9f3e7","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780993320619},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":96,"checkedAt":1789066325931},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill mostly matches Tushare financial-data use, but it also bundles credentialed web crawling, CAPTCHA OCR, broad local writes, and some broader-than-advertised datasets that deserve review before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"A Tushare token and outbound API calls are expected for financial data, but CI-style account/password login, CAPTCHA OCR, mass crawling, and repo documentation rewrites are more privileged than normal end-user finance queries.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation uses ordinary Python packages, but SKILL.md suggests pip install by package name and requirements.txt uses lower-bound versions, so dependency resolution is mutable rather than locked.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The main skill instructions disclose TUSHARE_TOKEN and Python API calls, but the bundled crawler uses TUSHARE_ACCOUNT and TUSHARE_PASSWORD plus outbound browser automation, and those higher-impact credentials and operations are not reflected in SKILL.md allowed-tools or artifact metadata requirements.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"I found no service, scheduled task, shell hook, or cross-session backdoor; local persistence is limited to user-invoked exports and documentation files written by the crawler, including arbitrary export paths in scripts/api_client.py.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"SKILL.md presents an end-user Tushare finance data helper, while README.md and scripts/crawl_docs.py add a documentation-sync crawler that logs into Tushare, solves CAPTCHA images, crawls many pages, and rewrites reference files; README.md also lists LLM-corpus and industry-economy endpoints beyond the narrower frontmatter description.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending queries and a Tushare token to Tushare. Do not run scripts/crawl_docs.py or enable the documented CI sync unless you intentionally want a headless browser to use Tushare account/password secrets and crawl/update local reference files. Use an isolated environment, pin dependencies, and choose export paths carefully.","findings":"[TP4] unexpected: Partially supported: the core skill is a Tushare finance/API helper, but the package also includes a disclosed maintenance crawler and broader reference endpoints not fully represented in the SKILL.md frontmatter.\n[LP1] unexpected: Supported for the crawler path: scripts/crawl_docs.py uses outbound Playwright browsing and TUSHARE_ACCOUNT/TUSHARE_PASSWORD, while declared runtime requirements only cover TUSHARE_TOKEN.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: Supported as a review concern for README.md's documented automated login, CAPTCHA OCR, large-scale documentation crawling, and PR-oriented synchronization workflow.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Supported: the artifact asks operators to configure Tushare account credentials for the crawler but provides little practical warning about CI secret exposure, account activity, or provider-policy implications.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Supported: automated CAPTCHA handling and credentialed browser login are unnecessary for ordinary financial-data retrieval, though they are disclosed as documentation-maintenance behavior rather than hidden payload execution.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: Supported in part for scope: reference docs include national policy, film, and other non-financial datasets; README.md discloses some of this breadth, but SKILL.md frames use mainly as financial-market and macroeconomic data.\n[SDI-1] expected: The API client's CSV/JSON/Excel export capability is disclosed in metadata/README and useful for data work, but it lacks path containment or overwrite warnings.\n[TT2] expected: The GITHUB_OUTPUT write in scripts/crawl_docs.py is consistent with GitHub Actions reporting and not independently malicious, but it is part of the higher-privilege crawler workflow.\n[T08] expected: The unpinned dependency finding is a valid supply-chain hardening issue, not evidence that the named dependencies or skill are malicious.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-only documentation is consistent with a Chinese Tushare finance dataset and is not a material security concern by itself.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789066325931}}}}}